(Filename: D:/Game Development/VoXR-Speech-Recognition/Runtime/Commands/VoxrCommandParser.cs Line: 441)

[VoxrCommandParser] Intent 'set_heading' has the pattern "orient to heading {heading}" and the longer "orient to heading {heading} mark {?elevation}", which extends it with the required literal "mark" in front of slot "{?elevation}". If that literal is dropped, the longer pattern loses that element's credit while the bare one still matches perfectly — so the bare one wins and the slot value the speaker did say is discarded silently. Make the literal optional ("?mark") so an otherwise-complete match reaches the same score with or without the word and wins on consumed span. That trade is not free: an optional literal also lowers the score of matches that are already missing something, and stops anchoring the slot behind it, which can then claim adjacent tokens.
